<AcademicLayout title="Yoolkyu Park | Research">
  <h1>Research</h1>

  <p>
    I am interested in mathematical and statistical methodology for spatially structured
    biomedical data, especially histopathology images and related imaging-derived
    measurements.
  </p>

  <p>
    Current interests include spatial statistics, topological data analysis, and
    computational methods for biologically meaningful problems. I am particularly
    interested in settings where mathematical structure and statistical inference remain
    central to the scientific question.
  </p>

  <h2>Fields of interest</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Spatial statistics</li>
    <li>Marked point pattern methods</li>
    <li>Topological data analysis</li>
    <li>Computational pathology</li>
    <li>Biomedical imaging</li>
    <li>Statistical methodology for structured biological data</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Current project</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="https://lce.biohpc.swmed.edu/sashimi/">SASHIMI</a>. Spatial analysis for
      AI-segmented histopathology images.
    </li>
  </ul>

